      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2016 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "We report a case of a 31-year-old woman with 2 previous caesarean deliveries who presented a diagnostic dilemma. She underwent caesarean section where she was found to have a uterine scar dehiscence with an adherent placenta and required a hysterectomy. While individually representing high risk to the mother and/or fetus, the combination in this case protected the fetus."
      },
